# Go golden files compare byte-for-byte — keep them LF on every platform.
face-go/internal/tui/testdata/golden/*.golden text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF everywhere: a CRLF shebang line ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") is not a
# shebang, and the failure reads as "bad interpreter" rather than "wrong line endings".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending-normalise (a corrupted GIF is a silent README regression).
*.gif binary
*.png binary

# Go sources must be LF in the WORKING TREE too, not just in the index. With core.autocrlf=true they
# check out CRLF on Windows, and `gofmt -l` then reports every file in the repo as unformatted --
# which makes gofmt useless locally and trains people to ignore it. The blobs are already LF, so this
# changes nothing in git history; it only fixes what lands on disk.
*.go text eol=lf

# The demo tour's inputs are hashed by face-go/internal/tui/demo_tour_test.go. The hashes are
# CR-stripped so a CRLF checkout cannot fake staleness, but keep these LF anyway: the tape and the
# fleet envelope are read INSIDE the VHS linux container, off this same working tree.
docs/assets/*.tape text eol=lf
docs/assets/demo-fleet.json text eol=lf
docs/assets/demo.manifest.json text eol=lf
